THE PREMISE -- is the 1-minute estimate less noisy?
================================================================================================================
  Split-half reliability: the window's changes split into interleaved
  odd and even steps, each half estimating the same quantity at the same
  time. Spearman-Brown corrects the half-length correlation up to full
  length. 1 - reliability is the estimator's noise share. A diagnostic,
  not a gate.
    vol_48    (48 steps)   half-correlation 0.7142   reliability 0.8333   noise share 16.7%
    vol_48_1m (1,440 steps) half-correlation 0.9863   reliability 0.9931   noise share 0.7%
    Spearman(vol_48, vol_48_1m) = 0.8719;  median ratio vol_48_1m / vol_48 = 0.1869
    (a random walk would give 1/sqrt(30) = 0.1826; a higher ratio is microstructure noise in the 1-minute prints)

